{"id": "q0076", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 224167610, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "Ryan’s allowance is $6 each week he completes his chores. He did his chores for 3 weeks. Then he bought ice cream cones for himself and 3 friends at $1.25 each. Now they all want to go to the movies and tickets cost $6.50 each. How many movie tickets can Ryan buy?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0076.wav", "input_sha256": "85265e889ec09eee95303cd65f7dc40cedeeaaef80067a53e8c9fcb50d52f509", "input_samples": 344600, "input_s": 21.538, "n_real_chunks": 22, "score": 0.2185, "act": 0.9993, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So Ryan's allowance is six dollars each week he completes his chores, and he did them for three weeks. That means he earned 6 times 3, which is 18 dollars total. Then he bought ice cream cones for himself and three friends at a dollar twenty-five each. That’s four people, so 4 times 1.2 5 equals five dollars. After buying the ice cream, he has 18 minus 5, which is 13 dollars left. Movie tickets cost six dollars fifty each, so we divide 13 by 6.5 0. That gives us about 1. 9, but since he can't buy a fraction of a ticket, he can only buy one movie ticket.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 21, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 32, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/aud